Totality Stomp
Ingredients: GRUNGE + EUPHORIC, ENERGETIC & JOLLY + Drums
Creative Catalyst: Descended from an itinerant caste of carnival musicians who perform only under the fleeting twilight of solar eclipses.

Totality Stomp is a cathartic, mud-spattered collision of Pacific Northwest drop-D grunge and unhinged traveling carnival fanfare. Built over relentless, double-time parade drum batteries, blown-out Russian fuzz pedals, and brass-band triumphant shouts, it transforms grunge's heavy catharsis into ecstatic, teeth-baring communal joy.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 145–175 BPM; a frantic, rolling 2/4 skank driven by pounding marching-band bass drums, battering un-damped snare drags, and syncopated floor-tom stomps.
- Harmonic Palette: Sludge-thick drop-D power chords juxtaposed against triumphant major pentatonic and Mixolydian fanfare melodies hammered out on battered accordions, brass, and slide guitar.
- Production Signatures: Ribbon microphones overloaded at the preamp stage to give acoustic drums an explosive, room-shaking saturation; dual-tracked calliope and kazoo horns blended seamlessly with searing Big Muff distortion; gang vocals recorded outdoors through megaphone horns.
- Dynamics: Violent, celebratory stop-start dynamics; verses strip back to solitary stomping kicks and grumbled fuzz-bass before detonating into confetti-blasting, euphoric choruses of polyphonic brass and snare flurries.

Scene & Origin Lore
Totality Stomp emerged from the dry orchard basins and abandoned airstrips of the Yakima Valley in the late 1990s, where seasonal carny-families cross-pollinated with flannel-clad, displaced garage punks. Bound by the nomadic tradition of the "Black-Sun Circuses"—itinerant performance troupes whose grand rituals occurred exclusively during celestial alignments—musicians gathered beneath brief midday twilights to unleash months of pent-up kinetic energy. Fashion in the scene mirrors this friction: grease-painted mechanic jumpsuits, welding goggles pushed back on sweaty foreheads, faded floral granddaddy shirts, and thrifted ringmaster swallowtail coats dusted with chalky orchard dirt. Shows are outdoor, daylight affairs that culminate in collective manic dancing, with festivalgoers trading self-pressed 7-inch records marked with astronomical coordinates.

Typical Instruments: Dual-station parade trap kits, vintage 28-inch marching bass drums, Ludwig Supraphonic snare drums, heavily distorted Fender Jazzmasters, Electro-Harmonix Russian Big Muff, button accordions, dented marching tubas, pawnshop trumpets, and bullhorns.

For Fans Of: Mudhoney, Gogol Bordello, The Polyphonic Spree, Dinosaur Jr.

